[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mB: events + fan-out (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mtask_event table written in-transaction, fan-out to notification rows in-process after commit. Event seam for [39m
     [38;5;246memail/push later, activity history for free, no queue infrastructure today.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m A: inline fan-out
     [38;5;246mNotification rows written directly in the update transaction. Fewest moving parts; no event stream, so email/push [39m
     [38;5;246mlater means reworking the notification path.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: derived inbox
     [38;5;246mNo notification rows; inbox is a query over events plus a last-read watermark. Smallest storage, but [39m
